-- K12's simulator: the list of the request's own test on the proof file's last chain, at a run.
/-
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/K12/Sim2/ListW.lean: CONDITIONAL. Two definitions (`IsListAtW`,
`LeftAtOwn`), and statements with their proofs.

Can the hypotheses be met together at a real run? NOT KNOWN. The head has members at the stored
files. That ready and runC return at a prover and a book with it, that the part is called, and that
a
value of `ThreadsP` is had there, is not shown here; nor, for the second statement,
that the maker returns at the wide filling (hAr). hleft is a premise, not discharged here, at that
filling. The wide filling (`onlineProverPartsInUse`) is defined in
Honest/K1/Law/WSideAtFill.lean.
`own_test_found_of_laid` and `onAtRun_W_at_return` call laws at it.
Two things are not shown here or beneath:
that W's rows are ready,
which bears on asks' last clause here;
and that the lent words are tied at the two shared tests
through `OnlineProverParts.through`.

What is here. `OnAtRun₃` (Honest/Law/OwedAtRun.lean: the condition On of one list of the last chain,
at a run that has returned, before a part that the run has called) at the list of the request's own
proximity test on the proof file's last chain (the place `placeW`, piece 2): the list's parts with
their simulators are `testPairs` of the job and the simulators' job behind the guard (`guardRow`);
its On is `OnOwnTestEntry` (Sim2/SlotOwnTest.lean). exact is held at the PAIR of that On and the bud
`budBoth Js`, at A := False, where the simulators' job names the declared first trees, and fresh
under a test on the book (`own_test_good`, the same file): `IsListAtW` pins all of that, and
`good_at_list_W` says it at the list's own On and bud. The fellow of `onAtRun_firstChainTest`
(Sim2/ListAtRun.lean) at the first chain's last test,
and of `onAtRun_own_key` (Sim2/RowOwnKeyAtRun.lean) at the key file.

  `IsListAtW`   the list: five equations: its place, its parts with their simulators, its On, its
      bud (`budBoth`, as in `own_test_good`), and the trees that the simulators' job names.
  `good_at_list_W`   at such a list `Good` at A := False, at the list's own On and bud: the form of
      the premise hand₃ of `owed_mute_of_threads_at_run` (Honest/Law/OwedAtRun.lean); not the field
      good of `owed_of_threads_at_run`: the list's own A and B are pinned by nothing. Its hB (no
      entry of the book is owned by a part of the test) is not discharged here.
  `LeftAtOwn`   what is left at one stand: two fields: asks · trees.
  `carriedAt_behind_guard`, `first_rounds_at_own_test`   two small laws; the first is a twin of
      `carriedAt_guarded` (Sim2/RowOwnKeyAtRun.lean, whose imports reach lean/E2E/).
  `onAtRun_W`   the statement at a free prover `G.prover H`, at any job M of several members whose
      numbers are the place's, whose first fold spends, and whose state on entry is `doorW`.
  `onAtRun_W_at_return`   the same where that prover is the one that the maker returns at the wide
      filling, at the job that `halfW` lays there (`jobRealW`).

THE END IS `OnAtRun₃` ITSELF: there the carried blocks ca are bound by carriedAt Bk k 2 … = .ok ca
at
the run's own coins k, and the stand m by the walk's own equation. No ∃ of this file's own stands in
an end. hleft is asked at EVERY m and ca, under these same hypotheses, and is handed besides where
the part stands (`StandsAt`), the invariant at the stand (`InsideOf` at T.I₃), what the stand has
seen, that the part was called, that the stand's input is the run's own, the five clauses that are
paid here (`FiveAt`), the clause door as it is paid here, and the rule's equation between the front
and the run's `beforeAt`.

THE PREMISES, SORTED. PUBLIC: h (the head). THE RUN: T (`ThreadsP`: the rule's own letter) · hρ (the
challenges have the declared form) · hR · hrun. WHICH OBJECTS: hp · hfr · hrec (the job: its
numbers,
that its first fold spends, its state on entry) · hs · ho · hJs (the simulators' job) · hL
(`IsListAtW`: the list). ON THE FILLING: hg (the half that the search finds at `placeW` in the
prover's last list is the job's, behind the guard; where L is the first list of G's last lists at
`placeW` it follows from hL and hp by `Sides.prover`'s text).

A TEST WITH CODE ON THE BOOK (a named Bool premise): hT (`tiesB`; at the maker's own book
`ties_for_atPure`, AtFullSide/K12/TiesForAtPure.lean, has it: not called).
AT THE RETURN, besides h, T, hρ, hR, hrun, hs, ho, hJs, hLs, hT, hleft as above. ON THE FILLING: hAr
(the maker returns Ar at the wide filling) · hL (that filling's last list is not empty: the
proposition `LastTestMade` (E2E/TheHonestProverStatements.lean, not imported) says it at its own
letters: a premise here) · hM (M is the job that `jobRealW` makes there)
·
hP (the rule's prover is the maker's: an equation between two terms; who lays G pays it). From hAr,
hL, hM, hP and the head's own places, chain and public part `own_test_found_of_laid`
(Sim2/FoundOwnAndShared.lean) pays hp, hfr, hrec and hg. THE PROVER ALONE IS THE RETURN's: the
description is the head's, and Bk is any book.
LEFT AT EVERY STAND: hleft (`LeftAtOwn`). ALL OF On's FIELD asks IS LEFT: `ShapeAsksD`'s
nine fields (six read the state on entry alone; plain, codes₁ and pub read the state behind the
batching and the first fold, which is made of the job's first state at the carried coins) and
`DataAsks`' four (cols, state, trees: equations on the job's own text; allSay ties the prover's
hidden words to the verifier's rows); NONE IS PAID HERE. Sim2/ListWThin.lean and
Sim2/ListWLines.lean
thin it.
  asks   `ShapeAsksD` and `DataAsks` at the job, at the stand's input, the part's own front, the
      carried coins and the challenges heard. Beside it, NOTHING
      CALLED: `OwnStand` (K12/AtFile/WStand.lean) holds lines, front (`FrontAsksD`) and saysAt
      (`SaysAt`) at a stand of a thread, TYPED AT OTHER LETTERS (frontOf m, restCoins of a row's
      coins; here restFront J m, carriedCoins of the carried blocks): no law that ties the two
      stands
      is shown here; `rows_at_own` (WFrontAsks.lean) pays tidy, dense and claims on records.
      WStand.lean's HEAD BEARS "NOT IN FRONT
      OF A LAW OVER COINS": whoever calls it here and keeps its letters takes that label.
  trees   `TreesAt` (Sim2/Clauses.lean): the trees that the job makes have the declared depths, and
      each column that the front lists of an opened tree is the job's tree's. AN EQUATION WITH THE
      FRONT. Beside it: `trees_at_job_own_test` (Sim2/TreesOwnTestJob.lean), from: the two
      senders of the first chain and the sending of Omega as the search finds them (the filling's) ·
      tests on the book (`k1CutFits` and its fellows, hnotO) · hheard: each challenge
      that W's rows' data hears stands in front of W's sender · hatO, ha', haskO on Omega's sender ·
      some forty public equations on shapes and codes. JOINED IN Sim2/ListWTrees.lean.

What the proof pays at every stand: that the field holds columns, at both parts
(`door_last_with_columns`) · le, leS, heardFit, heard, fold (`five_at_own_test`) · door, with no
patch: the job's own state function stands in (`door_at_own_test`): all Sim2/OwnTestEntry.lean.

AGAINST THE MEASURE "On: only equations that tie what is carried and the state to what stands in
front; it shuts out nothing that a real run takes; it must hold at all coins". On here is
`OnOwnTestEntry`: "the stand's field holds columns" and `OnEntry`, which is the library's
`OnFreeTD`, eight clauses, at a state function that agrees with the job's but for targets. BY
READING: the field's clause, le, leS, heardFit, heard speak of the stand and the front alone. door,
fold and trees are equations between what the job makes of the stand's input and the carried coins,
and what the front lists. door AND asks TOGETHER SAY: the affine rows that the front fixes (the rows
of the state on entry, which by door is a function of the front) are true of the hidden words that
the job makes of the index's reader, the table's randomness and the carried coins. `DataAsks`.allSay
IS THE ONE CLAUSE THAT TIES THE PROVER's HIDDEN WORDS TO THE VERIFIER's ROWS; the tests on the state
on entry read that state alone, values of that state among them; cols, state and trees hold at every
input and all coins where one public test passes (Sim2/ListWLines.lean). IT IS HARMLESS IF AND ONLY
IF hleft.asks IS A THEOREM AT ALL COINS: THIS FILE DOES NOT SHOW THAT.

THE FALL-BACK (`doorW` … `idleT12`): ARM (β). On shuts the fall-back state out at the second part:
`ShapeAsksD`.came asks that the state on entry holds a mask (K12/PlanBDense.lean), and `idleT12`
holds
none (K12/AtProof/Doors.lean). `doorW` falls back only where one of the three folds or the last
chain's start fails, or the way in refuses (K12/DoorLast.lean: five places); `enterOwn` never
refuses
(Johnson/Desc/K12/Seat/Own.lean: it is .ok of a record). THAT THE FALL-BACK IS NOT TAKEN AT A CALLED
PART IS NO PREMISE OF THE TOPS HERE, AND NO THEOREM OF THIS FILE: it is
`door_own_at_called` (K12/DoorLastAtRun.lean: the door is at hand at the stand's rounds and field,
at
both parts) and, with the state tied to the run's own fold and with came, `own_test_door_tied` and
`own_test_door_returns` (Sim2/ListWCame.lean). Of the walk and of a called part, not of play.
`exact_free_trees` is empty where the first fold sends its own table (by Sim/TreesExact.lean's head,
as it says): not so here: hfr: the first fold spends.

Limits. The rule moves the debt and pays none of it. The condition reads the input and the carried
values: no later law may take it as a hypothesis on a run and then speak of the random values as
sampled anew. Of the walk (runC), not of play. Rows stay at the base filling's types: no crossing is
typed here. The full size alone, and the format's second hash function alone. Nothing on completeness,
soundness or hiding.
No property is claimed.
-/
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K12.Sim2.SlotOwnTest
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K12.Sim2.OwnTestEntry
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K12.Sim2.FoundOwnAndShared
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K12.Sim2.Clauses
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K12.Sim.ExactFirstAtU
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.Law.OwedAtRun
import AtFullSide.K12.OpenTiesAtHeadWL
import Johnson.P5J.ChainFree

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

noncomputable section

namespace ProofFile.Honest.K12.Sim2
open VerifiableInference.Desc (Block Chain Place)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.K12 (T12)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.K12.Seat (enterOwn)
open H2K.Member (codesFull piWFull)
open H2K.Pub (sgOf)
open ProofFile.Honest ProofFile.Honest.K12 ProofFile.Honest.K12.AtProof ProofFile.Honest.K12.Light

variable {W₀ Rc Tr : Type}

/-- **The list of the request's own test**: five equations. bud: the bud at which exact is held
(`own_test_good`, Sim2/SlotOwnTest.lean). opens: the simulators' job names the trees that the test's
first round of positions opens, each at its declared depth: without it exact is not held
(`OpenTies`, Sim/TreesExact.lean). -/
structure IsListAtW {Bk : ProverCoinCounts} {S Cl Y : Type}
    (L : Lettered Bk S Cl (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y ProofFile.Inst)
    (J : TestJob (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y) (Js : SimJob ProofFile.Inst)
    (os : List (Fmt.Shape × Fmt.TreeSource)) : Prop where
  place : L.place = placeW
  row : L.row = guardRow (testPairs J Js)
  on : L.On = OnOwnTestEntry Face.own J Js codesFull 2 os
  bud : L.bud = budBoth Js
  opens : Js.opens = os.map fun x => ((srcOf 2 x.2).1, (srcOf 2 x.2).2, x.1.a)

/-- CONDITIONAL on the head, the jobs' letters, the list and hB. **AT SUCH A LIST exact IS HELD**:
`own_test_good` at the list's own On and bud. hB: a test on the book. At A := False: plays and acc
are
met for nothing. -/
theorem good_at_list_W {Z : VerifierAndGoals.PublicFiles} {D₀ : OnBytes.Maker.WholeD} {r₀ : LPFD.Full.RunPF}
    {Zp : ProofFile.Pub} {Np : H2U.Places4} {cF : Chain P5J.TS ProofFile.Cl}
    (h : P5J.AtMg OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D₀ r₀ Zp Np cF) {Y : Type} {Bk : ProverCoinCounts}
    (J : TestJob (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y) (Js : SimJob ProofFile.Inst) (hp : J.p = (fourOf Np).W)
    (hfr : J.fresh.isNone = false) (hs : Js.p = (fourOf Np).W) (ho : Js.own = false)
    (L : Lettered Bk (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃ (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl
      (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y ProofFile.Inst)
    (hL : IsListAtW L J Js (fourOf Np).W.nums.first)
    (fs : List (Fall (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃))
    (σ : Side (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃ (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl
      (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y ProofFile.Inst)
    (hσ : L.side (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder fs = some σ)
    (pre : List (ℕ × ℕ × List Fmt.DeclaredRound)) (ord : List Place) (firstTree : ℕ)
    (B : Coins Bk → (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃ → Mid (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y → Env →
        Prop)
    (hB : ∀ u ∈ σ.members, ProofFile.Honest.Small.noneSpent Bk ⟨σ.block.place, u.number⟩ = true) :
    Good pre Face.own σ Bk ord 2 firstTree (fun _ _ _ _ => False) B L.On L.bud := by
  rw [hL.on, hL.bud]
  refine own_test_good h J Js hp hfr hs ho Face.own 2 firstTree _ (by rw [first_head_W h]; rfl)
    (openTies_head_W h J Js hp 2 hL.opens) fs σ ?_ pre Bk ord B hB
  have hPW : J.p.place = placeW := by
    rw [hp]
    exact p12At_place _ _
  rw [hPW, ← hL.place, ← hL.row]
  exact hσ

/-- **What is left at one stand of the request's own test.** asks: ALL of the field asks of
`OnFreeTD`, at the job: of its thirteen clauses `DataAsks`.allSay alone is on values. trees: the
clause trees of `OnFreeTD`, to the
letter. A definition: a premise's form. -/
structure LeftAtOwn {Y : Type} (J : TestJob (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y) (K : OnBytes.Codes)
    (os : List (Fmt.Shape × Fmt.TreeSource)) (mem : ℕ → Stretch) (m : Mid (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y)
    (front : Before) : Prop where
  asks : ∃ Dp cc Rw, Dp.ts.length = os.length ∧
    ShapeAsksD J m.st.input (restFront J m) (carriedCoins J mem) (heardIn J m) K Dp ∧
    DataAsks J m.st.input (restFront J m) (carriedCoins J mem) (heardIn J m) Dp cc Rw
  trees : TreesAt J 2 os mem m front

/-- The carried blocks do not see the guard. A twin of `carriedAt_guarded`
(Sim2/RowOwnKeyAtRun.lean). -/
theorem carriedAt_behind_guard {V W X : Type} (Bk : ProverCoinCounts) (k : Coins Bk) (c : ℕ) (a : Addr)
    (p : Part V W X) : carriedAt Bk k c a p.needsField = carriedAt Bk k c a p := by
  unfold carriedAt
  rw [lendPart_guarded]
  rfl

theorem first_rounds_at_own_test : firstLen piWFull.nums.stages ≠ 0 := by decide +kernel

/-- CONDITIONAL on all its premises. **The clause of the rule at the list of the request's own test,
at a free prover.** -/
theorem onAtRun_W {Z : VerifierAndGoals.PublicFiles} {D₀ : OnBytes.Maker.WholeD} {r₀ : LPFD.Full.RunPF}
    {Zp : ProofFile.Pub} {Np : H2U.Places4} {cF : Chain P5J.TS ProofFile.Cl}
    (h : P5J.AtMg OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D₀ r₀ Zp Np cF) {Ky X₀ Y' : Type} {Bk : ProverCoinCounts}
    {H : Prover W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Ky Tr X₀ Y'}
    {G : Sides (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk W₀ Rc Ky Tr X₀ Y'} {w₀ : W₀} {rc : Rc}
    {x : ProofFile.Inst} {k : Coins Bk} {ρ : Draws} {R : Ready W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Ky Tr X₀ Y'}
    {r : RunC (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF)}
    (T : ThreadsP (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k R)
    (hρ : ρ.due (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) = true)
    (hR : ready (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k = .ok R)
    (hrun : runC (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k ρ = .ok r)
    -- the two jobs
    (M : ManyJob (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y') (hp : M.toRun.toTest.p = (fourOf Np).W) (f : Addr ×
              ℕ)
    (hfr : M.toRun.toTest.fresh = some f)
    (hrec : M.toRun.toTest.rec₀ =
      doorW (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) (·.x) enterOwn placeW idleT12)
    (Js : SimJob ProofFile.Inst) (hs : Js.p = (fourOf Np).W) (ho : Js.own = false)
    (hJs : Js.rec₀ = stateAtOwnTest OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF)
    -- the list
    (L : Lettered Bk (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃ (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl
      (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y' ProofFile.Inst)
    (hL : IsListAtW L M.toRun.toTest Js (fourOf Np).W.nums.first)
    -- on the filling
    (hg : ((G.prover H).second.find? fun g => g.place == placeW) =
      some ((proverSideOfProximityTest M.toRun.toTest : Placed (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr)
          Y').needsField))
    -- on the book: a test with code
    (hT : tiesB Bk placeW M.toRun.toTest.members.length = true)
    -- at every stand of the run: what is left
    (hleft : ∀ (m : Mid (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y')
      (ca : CsAll (restMember (V := Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) M.toRun.toTest Js).part.carries)
      (σ : Side (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃ (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl
        (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y' ProofFile.Inst)
      (pre' t' pre t : List (Block (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃
        (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl)),
      (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder = pre' ++ σ.block :: t' →
      Side.seated (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder placeW
        (guardRow (testPairs M.toRun.toTest Js)) [] = some σ →
      StandsAt (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder R.second σ
        (restMember M.toRun.toTest Js).guarded pre t (firstLen M.toRun.toTest.p.nums.stages) →
      InsideOf .own Bk 2 (G.prover H).second σ.block (T.I₃ pre'.length) (σ.roundsTo 1) k m
        (envOf (H.storedWords w₀ rc) (taken₃ r.run.played.1 r.run.played.2.1)
          (r.run.played.2.2.take ((pre'.flatMap (·.rounds)).length + σ.roundsTo 1))) →
      m.seen = roundsOf r.run.played.1 ++ roundsOf r.run.played.2.1 ++
        roundsOf (r.run.played.2.2.take ((pre'.flatMap (·.rounds)).length + σ.roundsTo 1)) →
      r.called ⟨L.place, 1⟩ = true →
      carriedAt Bk k 2 ⟨L.place, 1⟩ (restMember (V := Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) M.toRun.toTest
          Js).part =
        .ok ca →
      midAtW (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k ρ ⟨L.place, 1⟩ =
        .ok (some m) →
      m.st.input = R.own →
      FiveAt M.toRun.toTest (stretches _ ca) m
        (r.run.beforeAt (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked) ⟨L.place, 1⟩) →
      M.toRun.toTest.rec₀ m.st.input (restFront M.toRun.toTest m) =
        stateAtOwnTest OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF x
          ((r.run.beforeAt (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked) ⟨L.place, 1⟩).cut
            (firstLen M.toRun.toTest.p.nums.stages)) →
      (laidOf (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) ρ r.run.played.1 r.run.played.2.1
          (r.run.played.2.2.take ((pre'.flatMap (·.rounds)).length + σ.roundsTo 1))).front 2
          (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) (storedAsks (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) ρ)) =
        r.run.beforeAt (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked) ⟨L.place, 1⟩ →
      LeftAtOwn M.toRun.toTest codesFull (fourOf Np).W.nums.first (stretches _ ca) m
        (r.run.beforeAt (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked) ⟨L.place, 1⟩)) :
    OnAtRun₃ T ρ r L := by
  obtain ⟨hplace, hrow, hOn, -, -⟩ := hL
  intro σ hσ u hu pre' t' hcut m ca hin hseen hca hc hmid hfr'
  have hpl : σ.block.place = L.place := side_place hσ
  have hPW : M.toRun.toTest.p.place = placeW := by
    rw [hp]
    exact p12At_place _ _
  have hσ₀ : Side.seated (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder placeW
      (guardRow (testPairs M.toRun.toTest Js)) [] = some σ := by
    rw [← hplace, ← hrow]
    exact hσ
  have hσ' : Side.seated (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder M.toRun.toTest.p.place
      (guardRow (testPairs M.toRun.toTest Js)) [] = some σ := by
    rw [hPW]
    exact hσ₀
  have hg' : ((G.prover H).second.find? fun g => g.place == σ.block.place) =
      some ((proverSideOfProximityTest M.toRun.toTest : Placed (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr)
          Y').needsField) := by
    rw [hpl, hplace]
    exact hg
  have hfrN : M.toRun.toTest.fresh.isNone = false := by
    rw [hfr]
    rfl
  -- the members
  obtain ⟨b₀, hb₀, e₀⟩ := Option.map_eq_some_iff.1 hσ'
  have hbare : testSide (V := Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder
      M.toRun.toTest Js [] =
      some (⟨b₀, testPairs M.toRun.toTest Js, fallOf [] M.toRun.toTest.p.place⟩ :
        Side (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃ (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl
          (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y' ProofFile.Inst) := by
    unfold testSide Side.seated
    show Option.map _ ((P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder.find? fun b => b.place == _) =
        _
    rw [hb₀]
    rfl
  obtain ⟨hfit₀, hmem₀, -⟩ :=
    (first_any_head_W (V := Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) h M.toRun.toTest Js hp hfrN hs ho).2.2 [] _
        hbare
  have hmem : σ.members = [(firstMember M.toRun.toTest Js).guarded, (restMember M.toRun.toTest
      Js).guarded] := by
    rw [← e₀]
    show membersOf (guardRow _) 0 _ = _
    rw [membersOf_guardRow]
    exact congrArg (List.map Member.guarded) hmem₀
  have hrowσ : σ.row = guardRow (testPairs M.toRun.toTest Js) := by rw [← e₀]
  have hblk : σ.block ∈ (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder := by
    rw [← e₀]
    exact List.mem_of_find?_eq_some hb₀
  have hfitg : σ.fits = true := by
    rw [← e₀]
    show (⟨b₀, guardRow _, _⟩ : Side (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃
      (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) Y'
          ProofFile.Inst).fits = true
    rw [fits_guarded_row]
    exact hfit₀
  rw [hOn, hfr']
  rw [hmem] at hu
  have hc' : r.called ⟨σ.block.place, u.number⟩ = true := by
    rw [hpl]
    exact hc
  have hmid' : orRefused (midAtW (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k ρ
      ⟨L.place, u.number⟩) = .ok m := hmid
  rcases List.mem_cons.1 hu with rfl | hu'
  · -- the first part: the field holds columns
    have hpos₁ : (firstMember (V := Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) M.toRun.toTest
        Js).guarded.part.moves.length ≠ 0 := by
      show (firstPart M.toRun.toTest : Part (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr)
          Y').needsField.moves.length ≠ 0
      rw [needsField_length, ProofFile.Honest.K12.Light.first_moves_len, hp, (reads_head_W h).1]
      exact first_rounds_at_own_test
    obtain ⟨pre, t, S₀⟩ := stands_member_last h.laid.planOk hR σ hblk hfitg _
      (by rw [hmem]; exact List.mem_cons_self) hpos₁ _ hg' (by rw [hrowσ]; rfl)
    obtain ⟨m₂, e₁, e₂, v₀, s, cols, tr, hm₂, -, -, hop, -⟩ :=
      door_last_with_columns h.laid.planOk hR σ _ pre t _ S₀ hrun hc'
    rw [hpl] at hm₂
    rw [hm₂] at hmid'
    obtain rfl : m₂ = m := Except.ok.inj (show (Except.ok m₂ : Except Refusal _) = .ok m from hmid')
    exact ⟨⟨_, hop⟩, fun hn => by cases hn⟩
  obtain rfl := List.mem_singleton.1 hu'
  have hc₁ : r.called ⟨σ.block.place, 1⟩ = true := hc'
  -- where the second part stands
  have Fc := facts_head_W h
  rw [← hp] at Fc
  obtain ⟨s, next, rest, hst⟩ : ∃ s next rest, M.toRun.toTest.p.nums.stages = s :: next :: rest :=
      by
    have hform := Fc.form
    unfold formPubB at hform
    cases hs' : M.toRun.toTest.p.nums.stages with
    | nil => rw [hs'] at hform; cases hform
    | cons a l =>
      cases l with
      | nil => rw [hs'] at hform; cases hform
      | cons b' r' => exact ⟨a, b', r', rfl⟩
  have l2 : (restPart M.toRun.toTest : Part (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr)
      Y').moves.length =
      restLen M.toRun.toTest.p.nums.stages := by
    rw [rest_moves M.toRun.toTest s next rest hst]
    exact (List.length_map _).trans List.length_range
  have hpos : (restMember (V := Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) M.toRun.toTest
      Js).guarded.part.moves.length ≠ 0 := by
    show (restPart M.toRun.toTest : Part (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr)
        Y').needsField.moves.length ≠ 0
    rw [needsField_length, l2, hp, (reads_head_W h).1]
    exact rest_rounds_at_own_test
  obtain ⟨pre, t, S'⟩ := stands_member_last h.laid.planOk hR σ hblk hfitg
    (restMember M.toRun.toTest Js).guarded (by rw [hmem]; simp) hpos (proverSideOfProximityTest
        M.toRun.toTest).needsField hg'
    (by rw [hrowσ]; rfl)
  have eN : ((σ.row.take (restMember (V := Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) M.toRun.toTest
      Js).guarded.number).map
      (·.1.moves.length)).sum = firstLen M.toRun.toTest.p.nums.stages := by
    rw [hrowσ]
    show (firstPart M.toRun.toTest : Part (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr)
        Y').needsField.moves.length + 0 = _
    rw [Nat.add_zero, needsField_length, ProofFile.Honest.K12.Light.first_moves_len]
  rw [eN] at S'
  -- the three laws at the stand
  obtain ⟨c, m₁, hm₁, hca₁, hown, F5⟩ := five_at_own_test h hρ hR M.toRun.toTest hp f hfr
    (fun s w fr mem mem' hh => rowsMu_many M s w fr mem mem' hh) Js hs ho [] σ hσ' hg'
    (by rw [hPW]; exact hT) hrun hc₁ (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked)
  obtain ⟨m₂, hm₂, hdoor⟩ := door_at_own_test h.laid.planOk hR hrun M.toRun.toTest hrec σ _ pre t S'
      hc'
    (hpl.trans hplace)
  obtain ⟨m₃, e₁, e₂, v₀, s₃, cols, tr, hm₃, hinp, -, hop, -⟩ :=
    door_last_with_columns h.laid.planOk hR σ _ pre t _ S' hrun hc'
  obtain rfl : m₁ = m₂ := Option.some.inj (Except.ok.inj (hm₁.symm.trans hm₂))
  obtain rfl : m₁ = m₃ := Option.some.inj (Except.ok.inj (hm₁.symm.trans hm₃))
  rw [hpl] at hm₁ hca₁ F5 hdoor
  have hmid₂ : orRefused (midAtW (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k ρ
      ⟨L.place, 1⟩) = .ok m := hmid'
  rw [hm₁] at hmid₂
  obtain rfl : m₁ = m := Except.ok.inj (show (Except.ok m₁ : Except Refusal _) = .ok m from hmid₂)
  have hcaG : carriedAt Bk k 2 ⟨L.place, 1⟩ (restMember (V := Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr)
      M.toRun.toTest Js).part = .ok ca :=
    (carriedAt_behind_guard _ _ _ _ _).symm.trans hca
  obtain rfl : c.2.1.2.2 = ca := Except.ok.inj (hca₁.symm.trans hcaG)
  have Lf := hleft m₁ _ σ pre' t' pre t hcut hσ₀ S' hin hseen hc hcaG hm₁ hown F5 hdoor hfr'
  refine ⟨⟨_, hop⟩, onEntry_of_free Face.own _ _ _ 2 _ _ _ m₁ _ ?_⟩
  refine ⟨F5.le, F5.leS, F5.heardFit, F5.heard, ?_, F5.fold, Lf.asks, Lf.trees⟩
  rw [hJs]
  have hx : m₁.st.input.x = x := by rw [hinp]
  show _ = stateAtOwnTest OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF m₁.st.input.x _
  rw [hx]
  exact hdoor

/-- CONDITIONAL on all its premises. **The same at the wide filling's return** (see the head):
the prover is the one that the maker returns at that filling; the
job is the one that `halfW` lays there. hL: the filling's last list is not empty.
THE PROVER ALONE IS THE RETURN's: the description is the head's, and Bk is any book. -/
theorem onAtRun_W_at_return {Z : VerifierAndGoals.PublicFiles} {D₀ : OnBytes.Maker.WholeD} {r₀ : LPFD.Full.RunPF}
    {Zp : ProofFile.Pub} {Np : H2U.Places4} {cF : Chain P5J.TS ProofFile.Cl}
    (h : P5J.AtMg OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D₀ r₀ Zp Np cF)
    (I : WiderIn W₀) (S' : OnBytes.HonestTrace.Sz) (O : OnlineProverArguments)
    {Ar : OnlineProverWithDescription W₀ IndexCommitterCoins Cells Unit Unit}
    (hAr : onlineProverFromPublicFiles OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z.pol Z.lay Z.KL (onlineProverPartsInUse I OnBytes.secondHashFunction S' O) =
      .ok Ar)
    (hL : (secondW I OnBytes.secondHashFunction S' O Ar.Z Ar.G :
      List (Placed (Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) (Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) Unit)) ≠ [])
    {Bk : ProverCoinCounts} {H : Prover W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst OnBytes.TableKey Cells Unit Unit}
    {G : Sides (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk W₀ IndexCommitterCoins OnBytes.TableKey Cells Unit Unit}
    (hP : G.prover H = Ar.H) {w₀ : W₀} {rc : IndexCommitterCoins} {x : ProofFile.Inst} {k : Coins Bk} {ρ : Draws}
    {R : Ready W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst OnBytes.TableKey Cells Unit Unit}
    {r : RunC (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF)}
    (T : ThreadsP (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k R)
    (hρ : ρ.due (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) = true)
    (hR : ready (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k = .ok R)
    (hrun : runC (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k ρ = .ok r)
    (M : ManyJob (Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) Unit)
    (hM : jobRealW S' (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) enterOwn O.pile (K1.lotNo OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp)
      (fun w => ⟨w.trace, I.weights Zp w.w₀, w.rc⟩) (fun w => I.weights Zp w.w₀)
      (fun P w => randAt P w.rc) Zp Ar.G = some M)
    (Js : SimJob ProofFile.Inst) (hs : Js.p = (fourOf Np).W) (ho : Js.own = false)
    (hJs : Js.rec₀ = stateAtOwnTest OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF)
    (L : Lettered Bk (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃ (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl
      (Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) (Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) Unit ProofFile.Inst)
    (hLs : IsListAtW L M.toRun.toTest Js (fourOf Np).W.nums.first)
    (hT : tiesB Bk placeW M.toRun.toTest.members.length = true)
    (hleft : ∀ (m : Mid (Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) Unit)
      (ca : CsAll (restMember (V := Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) M.toRun.toTest Js).part.carries)
      (σ : Side (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃ (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl
        (Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) (Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) Unit ProofFile.Inst)
      (pre' t' pre t : List (Block (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).S₃
        (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).Cl)),
      (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder = pre' ++ σ.block :: t' →
      Side.seated (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder placeW
        (guardRow (testPairs M.toRun.toTest Js)) [] = some σ →
      StandsAt (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF).second.blocksInOrder R.second σ
        (restMember M.toRun.toTest Js).guarded pre t (firstLen M.toRun.toTest.p.nums.stages) →
      InsideOf .own Bk 2 (G.prover H).second σ.block (T.I₃ pre'.length) (σ.roundsTo 1) k m
        (envOf (H.storedWords w₀ rc) (taken₃ r.run.played.1 r.run.played.2.1)
          (r.run.played.2.2.take ((pre'.flatMap (·.rounds)).length + σ.roundsTo 1))) →
      m.seen = roundsOf r.run.played.1 ++ roundsOf r.run.played.2.1 ++
        roundsOf (r.run.played.2.2.take ((pre'.flatMap (·.rounds)).length + σ.roundsTo 1)) →
      r.called ⟨L.place, 1⟩ = true →
      carriedAt Bk k 2 ⟨L.place, 1⟩ (restMember (V := Local W₀ IndexCommitterCoins ProofFile.Inst Cells) M.toRun.toTest
          Js).part =
        .ok ca →
      midAtW (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) Bk (G.prover H) w₀ rc x k ρ ⟨L.place, 1⟩ =
        .ok (some m) →
      m.st.input = R.own →
      FiveAt M.toRun.toTest (stretches _ ca) m
        (r.run.beforeAt (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked) ⟨L.place, 1⟩) →
      M.toRun.toTest.rec₀ m.st.input (restFront M.toRun.toTest m) =
        stateAtOwnTest OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF x
          ((r.run.beforeAt (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked) ⟨L.place, 1⟩).cut
            (firstLen M.toRun.toTest.p.nums.stages)) →
      (laidOf (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) ρ r.run.played.1 r.run.played.2.1
          (r.run.played.2.2.take ((pre'.flatMap (·.rounds)).length + σ.roundsTo 1))).front 2
          (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) (storedAsks (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) ρ)) =
        r.run.beforeAt (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked) ⟨L.place, 1⟩ →
      LeftAtOwn M.toRun.toTest codesFull (fourOf Np).W.nums.first (stretches _ ca) m
        (r.run.beforeAt (storedShown (H.storedWords w₀ rc) r.run.storedAsked) ⟨L.place, 1⟩)) :
    OnAtRun₃ T ρ r L := by
  have hN := h.laid.places
  have hcF := h.laid.chain
  obtain rfl : Ar.Z = Zp := Except.ok.inj ((atPure_ok hAr).1.symm.trans h.laid.pub)
  obtain ⟨N, c, M', hN', hc', hM', hp, ⟨f, hfr⟩, hrec, hg⟩ :=
    own_test_found_of_laid I OnBytes.secondHashFunction S' O hAr hL
  obtain rfl : N = Np := Except.ok.inj (hN'.symm.trans hN)
  obtain rfl : c = cF := Except.ok.inj (hc'.symm.trans hcF)
  obtain rfl : M' = M := Option.some.inj (hM'.symm.trans hM)
  exact onAtRun_W h T hρ hR hrun M' hp f hfr hrec Js hs ho hJs L hLs
    (by rw [hP]; exact hg) hT hleft

